{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he was building a city.</b> He did not build for himself but only for his son, for he himself had no city or dwelling in the land. And because he was cursed by the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He, and whatever he would do would not prosper, Scripture said of him ויהי בונה עיר to indicate that all his days he was building the city, and therefore it did not say ויבן עיר but rather ויהי בונה עיר. And the generations of Cain and his deeds were written down to show and to make known that YHWH, blessed be He, is slow to anger, and He prolonged his days, for he begot sons and grandsons; thus explained the R. M. b. R. Nahman, z\"l."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:19.324571586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}